        "like": 2
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree. Several creators I know personally have deleted their own worlds as a form of self-protection. In some cases, the original local project data no longer exists, making it impossible to re-upload those worlds. I hope VRChat will also consider restoring such worlds from backups where possible.\n\nIt's important that this wrongful wave of BANs does not cause irreversible damage to the diversity of VRChat or to the motivation of its creators.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "6a24b18dfe83f7f1a6c7065c",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "6a168fe15a52cb2df0a0cf2f",
        "alias": "Advisory Lynx",
        "aliasID": "6a168fe25a52cb2df0a0cf32",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/efc2a7da9b9954f137b5d0d49c8a206a.png",
        "created": "2026-05-27T06:32:01.850Z",
        "name": "Crescent_Evil",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "crescent-evil"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2026-06-06T23:47:25.901Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6a244fc8fe83f7f1a6b3fa67",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a good suggestion.\n\nHowever, in cases where creators delete their own worlds out of fear of crossing vague and unclear boundaries, I do not think creators will dare to restore their worlds unless the official side properly explains the specific boundaries of what counts as “inappropriate content.”\n\nWhat would truly reassure creators is the establishment of clearer standards for what is considered inappropriate.\n\nFor example, content with explicit sexual expression, such as worlds containing models, images, or text that expose private body parts, or worlds containing sex toy props, should fall under enforcement.\n\nHowever, for worlds that express fetish-related themes, such as ASFR-type worlds, but do not contain the above elements, will they also be subject to the same enforcement?\n\nIn addition, the way violations are handled needs to be reviewed.\n\nThe current approach, where a world is immediately deleted and the account is suspended, is overly harsh. On top of that, since there is no clear explanation of which specific content in the world crossed the rules, creators may not be able to make the appropriate changes.\n\nWhen trying to avoid the same world being banned again, creators will most likely choose not to upload that world again at all.\n\nI understand that clearly listing every type of prohibited content is extremely difficult. However, pointing out the specific content in each individual case should be very easy, because the reported content itself is already the answer.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-06-06T16:50:16.470Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "(Translated by DeepL)\n\nThere are many worlds that were deleted by creators to avoid having their own accounts banned following the deletion of several worlds and the implementation of account bans.\n\nHowever, these worlds would likely have remained intact had it not been for the “BANWave.” And as you have stated, if you acknowledge that the series of bans was a mistake, I believe you should also take steps to restore the worlds that were deleted to avoid being banned.\n\nI hope you will confirm your intention to address this issue and provide information on a contact point for world restoration.\n\n（Reference:Official Statement by VRChat Japan  https://x.com/VRChat_JP/status/2063283329865257349?s=20 )\n\n（日本語）\n\nここ最近のワールドの削除、アカウントBAN措置を受けて自らのアカウントのBANを避けるためにクリエイター自らが削除してしまったワールドが存在します。\n\nしかし、これらのワールドは公式が「誤った措置だった」と認めたBAN Waveが無ければ今も残っていたことでしょう。ならば、BANを避けるために削除されたワールドの復旧対応も行われるべきと思います。\n\n対応に応じる旨と、ワールド復旧の為の問い合わせ窓口の案内がされることを期待しています。\n\n（参考の公式表明: https://x.com/VRChat_JP/status/2063283329865257349?s=20 )",
